This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:

   The user's single request (verbatim intent): *"Tui's overlay is stuck on the menu: picking a game never actually launches a run, and the window chrome around the board is dead too, so the minimize-to-pill button, the resize toggle, the How to Play guide and the sign-out confirmation all do nothing. Wire the whole session back up: starting a run, pausing when the agent needs you and resuming, restarting mid-run, and ending a shift cleanly, plus the window minimize/restore/resize behavior the README and the on-screen buttons describe, including saving progress so a run can resume on the next launch."*

   Concretely this means restoring, in the `/app` `tui-gamepigeon` overlay:
   - Launching a run from the menu/variation screens (click + `Enter`), plus deep-link (`?game=`) and host `gamepigeon:launch`.
   - Pause on host `gamepigeon:pause` (agent Stop hook) and resume on `gamepigeon:resume`; the `#return-prompt` pause dialog and its four buttons.
   - Restart mid-run (`r`, in-canvas ↻, end-card button) with README semantics: throw the save away, new randomized seed ≠ the replaced seed, empty action log.
   - End a shift cleanly (in-canvas ‹ menu control, `#inline-back`, host `gamepigeon:reset`): leave the save exactly as it was; natural completion shows the end card, submits trace + local score.
   - Window chrome: `#resize` (↗/↙ compact 600×850 ↔ expanded 830×900), `#hide` → 144×48 handheld pill (`body[data-mode="pill"]`), `#pill` click → restore to compact with a 500×700 minimum floor, `#shutdown`, pill dragging.
   - `#how-to-play` dialog (from menu/variations `[data-open-how-to-play]`, in-canvas `help`, and `#how-to-play-from-pause`) and `#signout-prompt` confirmation (from `#account-chip` while signed in).
   - Saving progress so a run resumes on next launch (`[data-resume]` button, `settings.resumeLastGame`).

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Bun + TypeScript (strict, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`), Tauri v2 shell (Rust) with an undecorated/transparent always-on-top window; browser preview mode via a bridge façade.
   - Overlay app is a single imperative module (`overlay/app.ts`) driving `#screen` innerHTML per `Screen` state (`gate|menu|variations|scores|settings|game`), with event delegation on `screenElement`.
   - Phaser 3 canvas scene for Restaurant Arena (`mountRestaurantArenaScene`) that owns its own ResizeObserver/teardown-and-reboot on resize; all in-game chrome is on-canvas except the DOM intervention panel.
   - `PlayableGame` gym-style contract (`reset/step/state/score/isOver/hasWon/tickMs/keymap/checkpointState`); the *shell* must drive `tick` on the `tickMs()` cadence.
   - `WorkerOrchestrator` (live model crew) which paces worker turns and steps `tick` itself; `pause()/resume()/start()/stop()`.
   - Recording: `StoredOverlayTrace` journal (seed + ordered actions) → schema-v2 chunks; mid-episode sealed flush every 5s; `EpisodeEndReason` union; `TraceActor` union; `queue_recording_chunks` Tauri command; `append_local_score` only for natural completions.
   - `localStorage` persistence: one `SavedGame` (`gamepigeon.arcade.active-game.v1`), rebuilt action-by-action by `restoreGame`.
   - Host→webview events dispatched from Rust via `window.eval`: `gamepigeon:launch|resume|pause|reset|auth-success|auth-error|sync-error|sync-success|worker-budget`.
   - Multi-holder pause gating (new `PauseGate`) so independent holds (agent/dialog/minimized) don't resume each other's pauses.

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`/app/README.md`** (read) — authoritative spec for save semantics, window sizes, hook behavior, score history. Critical rules: menu-exit leaves the save untouched; restart discards it and randomizes a *new* seed; sizes 600×850 / 830×900 / 144×48 / floor 500×700 must equal `tauri-bridge.ts` exports and `overlay/preview.html`.

