steps.message:
This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:

   Single user request (verbatim): *"Tui's overlay is stuck on the menu: picking a game never actually launches a run, and the window chrome around the board is dead too, so the minimize-to-pill button, the resize toggle, the How to Play guide and the sign-out confirmation all do nothing. Wire the whole session back up: starting a run, pausing when the agent needs you and resuming, restarting mid-run, and ending a shift cleanly, plus the window minimize/restore/resize behavior the README and the on-screen buttons describe, including saving progress so a run can resume on the next launch."*

   Concretely, in the `/app` `tui-gamepigeon` overlay: launching runs (click + `Enter`, `?game=` deep link, host `gamepigeon:launch`); pause/resume via host `gamepigeon:pause`/`gamepigeon:resume` with the `#return-prompt` card; restart mid-run (`r`, in-canvas ↻, end-card button) with README semantics (discard the save, new seed ≠ replaced seed, empty action log); ending a shift cleanly (in-canvas ‹, `#inline-back`, host `gamepigeon:reset`) leaving the save untouched, with natural completion showing the end card and submitting trace + local score; window chrome (`#resize` 600×850 ↔ 830×900, `#hide` → 144×48 pill, `#pill` restore with a 500×700 floor, `#shutdown`, pill dragging); `#how-to-play` and `#signout-prompt` dialogs; and saving progress so a run resumes next launch (`[data-resume]`, `settings.resumeLastGame`).

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Bun + TypeScript (strict, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`; no `noUnusedLocals`), Tauri v2 shell (Rust) with undecorated transparent always-on-top window; browser preview via a bridge façade.
   - `overlay/app.ts` is one imperative module driving `#screen` innerHTML per `Screen` (`gate|menu|variations|scores|settings|game`) with click delegation on `screenElement`.
   - Phaser 3 arena scene (`mountRestaurantArenaScene(parent, state, onAction, onUi)`); all in-game chrome is on-canvas except the DOM intervention panel.
   - `PlayableGame` gym contract (`reset/step/state/score/isOver/hasWon/tickMs?/keymap/checkpointState`); `tickMs()` returns 0 for every idle state (before doors open, open decision card, game over) so the shell re-reads it each schedule.
   - `WorkerOrchestrator` paces worker turns and calls `game.step("tick")` itself (bypassing `stepGame`), hence live-crew runs are not reproducible from seed + shell actions.
   - Recording: `StoredOverlayTrace` journal → schema-v2 chunks; 5s sealed mid-episode flush; `EpisodeEndReason = "game_over"|"won"|"lost"|"user_quit"|"restart"|"timeout"|"client_closed"|"engine_error"`; `TraceActor = "human"|"model"|"heuristic"|"random"|"environment"`; `buildOverlayGameResult` returns non-null only when `completedScore` is set.
   - Local score row via `invoke("append_local_score", { score: {...} })`; Rust validates `game_id` with `safe_recording_id(value, "game_")` (alphanumeric plus `_ - .`), `platform` ∈ {terminal, overlay}, `completed_at` must end in `Z`.
   - One `SavedGame` in `localStorage` key `gamepigeon.arcade.active-game.v1`, rebuilt action-by-action by `restoreGame`; `MAX_ACTIONS = 50_000`.
   - Host→webview events (Rust `window.eval`): `gamepigeon:launch` (`{game, variation}`), bare `pause`/`resume`/`reset`, `auth-success` (`{email}` only), `auth-error`, `sync-error`, `sync-success`, `worker-budget`.
   - Multi-holder pause gating via `PauseGate` (holds: `agent`/`dialog`/`minimized`).

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`/app/overlay/pause-state.ts`** (created in the prior session; unchanged here) — `PauseReason`, `PauseGate` (`hold/release/held/isPaused/reasons/clear`), `pausePrompt(run|null)` returning `{title, tone?, canContinue}`.

   - **`/app/overlay/persistence.ts`** (writers added in prior session; unchanged here) — `saveGame(save, storage = localStorage): boolean` (clears + returns false when `validSavedGame` fails), `clearSavedGame(storage)`, `loadSavedGame`, `restoreGame(entry, saved)`.

   - **`/app/overlay/tauri-bridge.ts`** (constants added in prior session; unchanged here) — `COMPACT_SIZE {600,850}`, `EXPANDED_SIZE {830,900}`, `PILL_SIZE {144,48}`, `MIN_SIZE {500,700}`, `OverlayWindowMode`, `overlayWindowSize(mode)`, and `applyOverlayWindowSize(overlayWindow, mode)` which sets **min size before size** and holds the single documented `as TauriLogicalSize` cast.

   - **`/app/overlay/app.ts`** (the main work; now ~1985 lines). Edits made this session:

     State added after `interveneRole`:
     ```ts
     /** True while the arcade is collapsed to the handheld pill. */
     let minimized = false;
     /** Everything currently holding the run still; see pause-state.ts. */
     const runPause = new PauseGate();
     /** The auto-advance timer for a run the shell paces itself. */
     let tickTimer: number | undefined;
     /** The seed the run on the floor was dealt, and what it has accepted so far. */
     let runSeed = 0;
     let runActions: string[] = [];
     /** The one modal on screen, if any. All three are mutually exclusive. */
     type DialogId = "pause" | "how-to-play" | "signout";
     let openDialogId: DialogId | undefined;
     ```
     `let gameSessionId: string | undefined;` was **removed**; the documented `sessionReceiptId` is now the run's single id (analytics subject, score `game_id`, receipt, trace export `sessionId`), set in `launchRun` as `sessionReceiptId = activeTrace.gameId;`.

     Window-frame section (inserted before `drawGate`): `windowMode()`, `applyWindowFrame()`, `renderResizeControl()` (↗/↙ + aria-label swap), `toggleWindowSize()`, `minimizeToPill()` (sets `minimized`, `document.body.dataset.mode = "pill"`, `holdRun("minimized")` **before** `closeDialog()`, `persistRun()`, `applyWindowFrame()`, focuses `#pill`), `restoreFromPill()` (clears mode, re-frames, re-opens the pause card when `runPause.held("agent") && screen === "game"`, then `releaseRun("minimized")`), `bindPill()` (pointerdown records origin and resets `dragged`; pointermove past 4px calls `windowHandle.startDragging()`; click ignored once if it ended a drag), and `bindWindowChrome()` (binds `#resize`, `#hide`, `#shutdown` → `persistRun(); endRun("client_closed"); void invoke("shutdown")`, plus `bindPill()`).

     Run-lifecycle section (before `moveMenuCursor`): `SEED_LIMIT = 2 ** 31`; `randomSeed(replacing?)` (never returns the replaced seed); `isEnvironmentAction(action)` (`tick`/`bot_move`); `clearTickTimer()`;
     ```ts
     function scheduleRun(): void {
       clearTickTimer();
       if (!game || gameEnded || replaying) return;
       // A game with no `tickMs` never advances on its own; it waits for the player.
       const interval = runPause.isPaused() ? 0 : game.tickMs?.() ?? 0;
       if (workerOrchestrator) {
         if (interval > 0) workerOrchestrator.start();
         else workerOrchestrator.pause();
         return;
       }
       if (interval <= 0) return;
       tickTimer = window.setTimeout(() => {
         tickTimer = undefined;
         if (!game || gameEnded || runPause.isPaused()) return;
         performAction("tick");
       }, interval);
     }
     function holdRun(reason: PauseReason): void { runPause.hold(reason); clearTickTimer(); workerOrchestrator?.pause(); }
     function releaseRun(reason: PauseReason): void { if (!runPause.release(reason)) return; scheduleRun(); }
     ```
     `persistRun()` (writes `SavedGame` with `ownerId: signedInUser()?.id ?? ""`, `seed: runSeed`, `actions: [...runActions]`; **clears the save instead when a `workerOrchestrator` is driving**, because the orchestrator's turns never pass through `stepGame`); `LaunchOptions {seed?, restored?}`; `launchRun(selected, variationIndex, options)` (calls `endRun("user_quit")` first, resets counters, creates the trace, re-journals restored actions with the `isEnvironmentAction` rule, `attachWorkerOrchestrator`, `captureOverlayEvent("game.started", …, sessionReceiptId)`, `renderGameScreen(); persistRun(); scheduleRun();`); `launchById(gameId, variationId?)` (unknown/missing variation → index 0); `resumeSavedGame()` (drops the record and returns false when the game/variation/version no longer matches or the restored run `isOver()`); `restartRun()` (`closeDialog(); endRun("restart"); clearSavedGame(); launchRun(…, { seed: randomSeed(replaced) })`); `leaveToMenu()` (`persistRun(); endRun("user_quit"); closeDialog();` then menu — save untouched); `endRun(reason)` (clears timers/flush/orchestrator/scene, `runPause.clear()`, `submitTrace` only `if (activeTrace && !gameEnded)`, `game = undefined; gameEnded = true`); `finishRun()` (idempotent via `gameEnded`, clears the save, `submitTrace(activeTrace, won ? "won" : "lost", score)`, `captureOverlayEvent("game.ended", {...})`, `invoke("append_local_score", { score: { game_id: sessionReceiptId, …, platform: "overlay" } })`, then `showGameEndOverlay`); `showGameEndOverlay(score, won)` (appends `.game-end-overlay` with `data-tone` into `.board`, composing `getArenaDebriefHtml()`, `getArenaEvidenceHtml()`, `getArenaTimelineHtml()`, `sessionReceiptHtml()`, `[data-restart]`, `[data-menu]`, and the `.export-trace-group` buttons); `handleSceneUi(action)` deferring menu/restart/help through `window.setTimeout(…, 0)` so the Phaser emitter isn't destroyed mid-dispatch.

     Dialogs section: `DIALOG_SELECTORS` (`pause`→`#return-prompt`, `how-to-play`→`#how-to-play`, `signout`→`#signout-prompt`), `dialogElement`, `howToPlayReturnsToPause`, `renderPauseCard()` (writes `#return-title`, `data-tone`, hides `#continue-game` per `pausePrompt`), `openDialog(id)` (hides any previous card, `holdRun("dialog")`, focuses first button), `closeDialog()` (`releaseRun("dialog")`), `closeHowToPlay()` (returns to the pause card when opened from it), `backToCoding()` (`holdRun("agent"); closeDialog(); windowHandle.hide()`), `resumeFromPause()` (`releaseRun("agent"); closeDialog()`), `confirmSignOut()` (on `signOut()` failure rewrites `#signout-title` and keeps the card up; on success `persistRun(); endRun("user_quit"); clearSavedGame(); clearSignInPending(); closeDialog();` resets `entry/cursor/localScores` and `drawGate()`), `bindDialogs()`, `handleDialogKey(event)` (Esc: pause→backToCoding, guide→closeHowToPlay, else close; Enter: signout→confirm, guide→close, else backToCoding; `m` on the pause card → `leaveToMenu()`).

     Other modifications: `drawGame()` now `if (game.isOver()) finishRun(); else scheduleRun();`; `performAction` uses `isEnvironmentAction` and `if (result.moved) persistRun();`; `stepGame` pushes only moved actions into `runActions`; `renderGameScreen` passes `handleSceneUi` as the scene's `onUi`; `handleMenuKey` `quit` → `minimizeToPill()`; `handleVariationKey` `enter` → `launchRun(entry, variationCursor)`; `handleGameKey` handles `quit` → pill and `r` → `restartRun()` (works on the end card) before the `isOver()` guard; keydown listener gained dialog routing, pill Enter/Space restore, and global `Escape` → pill; click delegation gained `#inline-back` in game → `leaveToMenu()`, `data-open-how-to-play`, `data-resume`, `data-restart`, `data-menu`, `data-variation-index`; `#account-chip` opens the signout dialog when signed in; host-event listeners for `launch/pause/resume/reset/auth-success/auth-error/sync-error/sync-success` (pause card suppressed when `minimized` or `screen === "gate"`); `unlockTui` now calls `openInitialScreen()`; new `adoptSavedGame(ownerId)` and `openInitialScreen()` (deep link → resume setting → menu); boot calls `bindWindowChrome(); bindDialogs();` and, inside `loadSettings().then`, `renderResizeControl(); applyWindowFrame();`.

   - **`/app/overlay/pause-state.test.ts`** (created) — 7 tests: hold/release return values, "closing a dialog cannot resume a shift the agent paused", releasing an unheld reason, `clear()`, and the three `pausePrompt` cases.

   - **`/app/overlay/persistence.test.ts`** (created) — fake injectable `Storage` (with a `failWrites` mode); round-trip, single-record overwrite, quota failure returns false, clear, `MAX_ACTIONS` overflow drops the record, corrupt/invalid JSON, and `restoreGame` cases (replays to `episode.tick === 2`; rejects foreign gameId, wrong `gameVersion`, unknown action).

   - **`/app/overlay/tauri-bridge.test.ts`** (created) — asserts the four exact sizes, `overlayWindowSize` min pairing, and via a recording fake window that `applyOverlayWindowSize` emits `["min 144x48","size 144x48"]`, `["min 500x700","size 600x850"]`, `["min 500x700","size 830x900"]`.

4. Errors and fixes:
   - `overlay/app.ts(1233,46): error TS2722: Cannot invoke an object which is possibly 'undefined.'` — `tickMs` is optional on `PlayableGame`. Fixed with `const interval = runPause.isPaused() ? 0 : game.tickMs?.() ?? 0;` plus a comment ("A game with no `tickMs` never advances on its own").
   - Redundant duplicate run-id state (`gameSessionId` identical to `sessionReceiptId`) — removed `gameSessionId` and routed the analytics subject and score `game_id` through `sessionReceiptId`; verified with typecheck + tests.
   - Design hazards resolved before they became bugs: `minimizeToPill` originally closed the dialog before taking the hold (would briefly resume the run) → hold first; the pause card over the gate would swallow the `Enter` that starts sign-in → suppressed there; scene-originated menu/restart destroying Phaser mid-dispatch → deferred via `setTimeout(0)`; orchestrator started before the doors open would advance the night → `scheduleRun` gates the orchestrator on `tickMs() > 0`.
   - Pre-existing/baseline test noise (not caused by these changes, confirmed): `bun test ./src/` 4 failures, all AppleDouble `._*.test.ts` resource-fork parse errors; `bun run test:overlay` 2 failures — `overlay/recording.test.ts > only ever extends the sealed prefix as an episode continues` (5s timeout) and `scripts/plugin-update.test.ts > keeps the Claude marketplace install on its own updater` (imports nothing from `overlay/`).
   - No user feedback or corrections were received in this session (no user turns other than the continuation prompt and the final summary instruction).

5. Problem Solving:
   - Reconstructed the deleted region of `app.ts` from surviving evidence: unused declarations, the scene's `onUi` stub, `package.json` test paths, checked-in shell HTML ids/CSS, README guarantees, and the Rust command/event contracts.
   - Chose exactly one clock owner per run (shell timer vs orchestrator) and made every repaint re-enter the scheduler, which also explains the pre-existing comment in `submitIntervention` ("drawGame() re-enters the selected scheduler").
   - Prevented double score submission: `finishRun` is idempotent, clears the save, and a restored-but-finished run is treated as spent.
   - Honesty about save fidelity: a live-crew run keeps **no** save record rather than one that would resume a different night.
   - Verified end state: `bun run typecheck` clean; 21/21 new tests pass; `bun run build:overlay:web` regenerates `overlay/dist/app.js` containing the new code.

6. All user messages:
   - *"Tui's overlay is stuck on the menu: picking a game never actually launches a run, and the window chrome around the board is dead too, so the minimize-to-pill button, the resize toggle, the How to Play guide and the sign-out confirmation all do nothing. Wire the whole session back up: starting a run, pausing when the agent needs you and resuming, restarting mid-run, and ending a shift cleanly, plus the window minimize/restore/resize behavior the README and the on-screen buttons describe, including saving progress so a run can resume on the next launch."* (carried into this session via the continuation prompt)
   - A final system-level instruction directing that this turn produce a text-only summary with no tool calls.
   - No security-relevant instructions or constraints were stated.

7. Pending Tasks:
   - Finish the last verification thread: confirm the arena's DOM chrome (`.arena-worker-mode` z-index 40, `.arena-intervene-toggle` 40, `.arena-intervene-panel` 41) does not sit above `.game-end-overlay` (z-index 5) on the end card; if it does, raise the end overlay's stacking (e.g. an inline `z-index` on the appended element) or hide the intervention chrome once `gameEnded`.
   - Deliver the final report to the user, explicitly stating: (a) the `auth-success`/`auth-error`/`sync-*` listeners were added slightly beyond the literal list because sign-out without them would strand the user at an unusable gate; (b) the replay feature (`lastReplay`, `replaying`) was deliberately left unimplemented as out of scope, so `lastReplay` remains unused; (c) `setHud` remains unused pre-existing code; (d) live-crew (model-driven) runs intentionally keep no save record; (e) the two `test:overlay` failures and four `src` failures are pre-existing baseline noise with the exact reasons.

8. Current Work:
   All code and tests are written, typechecked, passing, and bundled. The immediately preceding action was a CSS stacking-order sanity check on the newly added end card: `grep -n "z-index" overlay/dist/index.html` then reading lines 910-918 and 940-968, which showed `.arena-worker-mode { z-index: 40 }`, `.arena-intervene-toggle { z-index: 40 }`, `.arena-intervene-panel { z-index: 41 }`, versus `.game-end-overlay { position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 5 }` (line ~1834). Since `showGameEndOverlay()` appends the card into the same `.board` (`.arena-stage`) element that contains that chrome, the worker-mode line, the intervene toggle and its panel would paint over the end card. This was unresolved at the moment of the summary request.

9. Optional Next Step:
   Resolve the stacking issue found in that last check by giving the appended end card a stacking context above the arena's DOM chrome (e.g. set `overlay.style.zIndex = "50"` in `showGameEndOverlay`, or hide the intervention toggle/panel once the shift is over), then re-run `bun run typecheck`, `bun test overlay/pause-state.test.ts overlay/persistence.test.ts overlay/tauri-bridge.test.ts`, and `bun run build:overlay:web`, and report completion with the caveats listed in Pending Tasks. This is the direct continuation of *"Wire the whole session back up: … and ending a shift cleanly"* — the end card is what a naturally completed shift shows.

If you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /logs/agent/sessions/projects/-app/5d384789-90da-4025-b6f6-a25491cc6895.jsonl
Continue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with "I'll continue" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.
